# The archive files are 8-bit ND data, NOT text. Their line terminator is a
# parity-carrying CR (0x8D) followed by LF. If git applied its usual
# LF->CRLF translation it would insert a second, plain CR and corrupt the
# originals. Mark every data file binary so git stores the bytes verbatim.
*.SYMB   -text
*.ORG    -text
*.BPUN   -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF endings or bash rejects them under WSL.
*.sh     text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.c      text eol=lf
*.h      text eol=lf
